## Completed: MS MARCO Passage Search App

### What was built

**Backend**: Anserini 2.1.1 fatjar with REST API server on port `8080` (configurable via `BACKEND_PORT` env var)
- Index: `msmarco-v1-passage` (MS MARCO V1 passage corpus)
- Endpoint: `GET /v1/msmarco-v1-passage/search?query=...&hits=...`
- Response includes `docid`, `score`, `rank`, and `doc` (passage text)

**Frontend**: Next.js 16 (Turbopack) on port `3000` (configurable via `FRONTEND_PORT` env var)
- `src/app/page.tsx` — Main page with search input, 5 randomly selected sample queries (from a pool of 10 MS MARCO passage dev queries), and ranked result display
- `src/app/api/search/route.ts` — API proxy that forwards requests to the Anserini REST server
- Handles empty queries (400), no results, and backend errors (502/503)

**Sample queries** (hardcoded from `msmarco-v1-passage.dev`):
- "what is disease models", "types of java fonts", "how does genome editing work", "price chopper locations in ct", etc.

